5
00:00:07,288 --> 00:00:09,040
From a single photo.

6
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,293
In Puno, Peru,

7
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:12,320
nearly four thousand metres up,

8
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:13,920
nightly frost and extreme

9
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,800
sun tear roads apart.

10
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,880
Yet inspections are still done on foot,

11
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,520
with a tape and a notebook.

12
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:21,440
Severity is a judgement call,

13
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,000
budgets can't be audited,

14
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:25,440
and every repair closure pushes traffic onto

15
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:27,520
streets with no room to spare.

16
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,360
Meet PaveLens AI.

17
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,120
One photo. One scale.

18
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:34,760
One click. Meta SAM 3.1 takes plain words,

19
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,360
like pothole or crack,

20
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,360
and returns the true

21
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,320
outline of every distress.

22
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,680
Each outline is projected onto the road plane,

23
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:44,320
so areas come out in real square metres.

24
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,760
Then Muse Wonder takes

25
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,200
charge as the coordinator.

26
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,400
It calls nine specialised tools,

27
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:52,440
classifies each distress by ASTM severity,

28
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:54,320
and writes the repair protocol.

29
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:55,920
Every call is traced:

30
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:58,120
