31
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:59,920
And an independent reviewer flags

32
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:01,600
what an engineer should check.

33
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,280
Here's what makes it trustworthy:

34
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:05,467
the AI never invents a number.

35
00:01:05,507 --> 00:01:06,613
The condition index,

36
00:01:06,653 --> 00:01:08,760
the quantities and the budget in soles

37
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:11,160
all come from tested engineering code.

38
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,880
Enter a depth measured on site,

39
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,640
and everything recalculates.

40
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:15,880
Need to close the street?

41
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:18,480
PaveLens solves a Wardrop traffic equilibrium

42
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,120
on a demo network of Puno,

43
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:22,320
and finds the cheapest time to work.

44
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:23,840
Here, working at night cuts the

45
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:25,440
cost to drivers from four hundred

46
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:27,920
and fifty-six soles to seventy-three.

47
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:29,440
The result: a survey that

48
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:31,800
starts with a ninety-second analysis,

49
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:33,880
consistent from one inspector to the next,

50
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:36,480
and auditable down to the last square metre.

51
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,520
Built for cities with a

52
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:39,347
phone and a small budget.

53
00:01:39,387 --> 00:01:42,720
PaveLens AI. Meta models see the damage.

54
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,200
Engineering measures it,

55
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,120
